/Title (These charts are used to visualize the internal composition of a total value by breaking it down into sub-categories. They provide a clear view of how different components contribute to the overall sum, while still allowing for a primary comparison of total volumes across different data points.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1539 0 R
/Next 1543 0 R
>>
endobj
1543 0 obj
<<
/Title (Treemaps are used to display large sets of hierarchical data through nested rectangles of varying sizes. This visual is effective for ranking categories and identifying dominant patterns within complex datasets, where the area of each rectangle is proportional to the value it represents.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1539 0 R
/Prev 1542 0 R
>>
endobj
1544 0 obj
<<
/Title (These charts are used to perform side-by-side comparisons between multiple data series across distinct categories. They are designed to highlight differences and variances between groups, making it easy to identify trends and compare individual values directly within a single view.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1541 0 R
/Next 1545 0 R
>>
endobj
1545 0 obj
